 "display": {
  "title": "Episode 203: The Tall Chanukah Candles (Chanukah)",
  "title_basis": "master_catalog",
  "summary_short": "A Chanukah show with singer Eli Lipsker, Shema with three young guests, the story of the Rebbe Rashab's three-foot Chanukah candles, and the mezuzah contest finalists.",
  "summary_long": "Broadcast during Chanukah 5746. Uncle Yossi opens with the message of the Chanukah lights: as we sit and gaze at the flames, they speak of emunah and bitachon in Hashem, the G-d of miracles, and we pray that next Chanukah will be in Yerushalayim with the third Beis HaMikdash. Singer Eli Lipsker visits Studio 604 and sings 'Oy Chanukah', 'I Have a Little Dreidel' and 'Sevivon'. Three young children lead the Shema. The story tells of Naftali, a Chassid who danced with special joy every Chanukah. Before a winter journey, the Rebbe Rashab told him to buy Chanukah candles three feet tall. Stranded by a blizzard on the first night, Naftali was caught by robbers who told him to say his last prayers; he climbed onto his wagon and lit the tall candles, and fire watchmen in a distant tower saw the flames and galloped over, scaring the robbers away. Uncle Yossi then reads the list of finalists in the My Mezuzah contest, announces a 'Wonderful World of Shabbos' exhibit, and closes with Chanukah wishes.",
  "lesson": "Hashem gives a tzaddik special power to help those who turn to him, and the Chanukah lights remind us that Hashem is the G-d of miracles.",
